---
import PolicyLayout from '~/layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/config/site';
import { ADS } from '~/config/ads';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Which cookies Formatoza and its advertising partners use, why, and how to manage your consent and privacy choices."
  path="/cookies/"
  h1="Cookie policy"
  lead={`${SITE.name} does not set its own cookies. This page explains the cookies used by advertising partners and how to control them.`}
  updated="September 25, 2026"
>
  <h2>Cookies set by {SITE.name}</h2>
  <p>
    None. The converters need no cookies: files are processed in your browser and nothing about them
    is stored. The site does not use local storage to track you.
  </p>
  <h2>Advertising cookies</h2>
  <p>
    {ADS.enabled
      ? 'We show ads served by Google AdSense.'
      : 'When advertising is enabled, ads are served by Google AdSense.'}{' '}
    Google and its partners may set cookies (such as <code>__gads</code>, <code>__gpi</code> and{' '}
    <code>IDE</code>) or use similar technologies to deliver and measure ads, prevent fraud and —
    only with consent where required — personalise ads. See
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" rel="noopener">
      how Google uses cookies
    </a>{' '}
    for the current list and their purposes.
  </p>
  <h2>Consent</h2>
  <p>
    In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, a consent message from a
    Google-certified consent management platform asks for your choice before advertising cookies are
    used for personalisation. The page sets consent to “denied” by default for those regions before
    any advertising code loads.
  </p>
  <h2>Managing your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Use “Privacy choices” in the site footer to review or change your consent (available when
      advertising is active).
    </li>
    <li>
      Manage personalised ads in{' '}
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">
        Google Ads Settings
      </a>
      .
    </li>
    <li>
      Block or delete cookies in your browser settings; the converters keep working without cookies.
    </li>
  </ul>
</PolicyLayout>
